# Maps writers

Read `specs/maps.md` before editing. Maps is four clerk operations. Quote the operation you are changing.

| Op                | Allowed writers                                                                                                             |
| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Open District Map | `MapTileBootstrap`, `GoogleMapTilesImageryLayer`, `GoogleMapTileSessionService`, `MapCameraHost`                            |
| Plot places       | `MapMarkerHost` (only `ImageryLayer.Markers` assigner), `MapDistrictLayers` → `MapMarkers`, `MapMarker` / `MapMarkerLabels` |
| Draw path         | `RouteDrivePathRefresher`, `MapRouteTrail`, `MapRouteTrailLayer`                                                            |
| Validate address  | `PlacesAddressBox`, `MapsGeoService` / Places — pin only after `LocationCoordinate.IsValidated`                             |

Do not:

- Add OSM, `mt1.google.com`, or a second `ImageryLayer` on the same `SfMap`
- Return an empty `GetUri` while a Google `UrlTemplate` is live (resolve `2dtiles` or remove the override)
- Geocode inside a plot path
- Merge Map Tiles, Address Validation, Places, Routes, and Route Optimization
- Edit `MappingService.cs` for maps
- Enable `IsLiveTrackingEnabled`
- Invent a new tile/marker/polyline writer “to make another host work”

Three hosts (District Map, school pick, stop/home pick) must call the same bootstrap + marker host + trail APIs.

Guest tile proof: `MapsConnectionProbe` + `Tools/SfMapTileProbe google-urltemplate` + `MapTileBootstrap Host=DistrictMap Outcome=…`.

Do not restore `Documentation/Archive/2026-09-Maps-Competing-Writers/` (`MapInteractionDiagnostics`, `EligibilityRoutePdfBuilder`, OSM probe, duplicate `map-tile-probe`, diag smoke). Harness OSM stays in `Tools/SfMapTileProbe` only.
